bc250-vaapi (0.5.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Runtime dynamic dlopen probing for libx264 and libx265 to eliminate DT_NEEDED SONAME lock-in.
  * 32-bit multiarch library path resolution for Steam Link companion driver.
  * Multi-user telemetry permissions fallback to per-UID shared memory buffers.
  * DMA-BUF file descriptor leak fixes on Vulkan memory allocation failures.
  * Thread and slice command-line flag parser honoring BC250_MAX_CPU_THREADS.
  * Bounded NAL bitstream assembly preventing buffer overrun on payload spikes.
  * Pthread condition variable lifecycle cleanup on initialization failures.
  * Hardened zero-latency single-frame contracts for live and offline VA-API pipelines.

 -- BC-250 Project Contributors <support@bc250.org>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0530

bc250-vaapi (0.5.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add libx265 CPU fallback encoding for 100% 3D gaming contention isolation.
  * Native zero-copy DMA-BUF importation with safe fallback on unsupported memory.
  * Real-time network dynamic bitrate smoothing without QP jitter.
  * Chromium / Firefox hardware decode entrypoints for VP9 and AV1.
  * HDR10 to SDR tone-mapping post-processing pipeline.
  * Half-pel fractional motion estimation refinement and 2-frame B-frame GOP.

